{"kind":"request","text":"RC-1: a class for each refusal reason. This places planner\nrequest acf85bfa, with its corrections f72736d6 and e51c1c7e.\nBuild after the cutover head (05d618e2) lands, first of the small\nclient heads, ahead of PG-1, IE-1 and FG-1.\n\nWork:\n1. Beside `REFUSAL_REASONS` in `packages/bytes/src/records.ts`,\n   export a table of type `Record\u003cRefusalReason, RefusalClass\u003e`.\n   A reason with no class must fail to compile. Count the\n   reasons at the landed cutover head, because the cutover adds\n   `wrong-genesis` and `genesis-conflict`.\n2. Three classes: `never`, `head` and `protocol`, as acf85bfa\n   defines them.\n3. For each reason of class `never`, state in the note the\n   property that makes it hold at every later head, with the\n   file and line of the judge that gives it. Add a test for each:\n   a judge that refuses the bytes with that reason refuses them\n   with that reason at a later head.\n4. When you cannot state the property of a reason, class it\n   `head`. `head` is the safe class: a client keeps the request\n   until `notAfter`.\n5. Before you build, send me the proposed class of every reason\n   in one act, as a table. I confirm it in one act.\n\nThe head changes no answer. If the table is kernel source under\ndocs/kernel.md section 7, say so in the note and ask for that\nreview.","body":{"conditions":"Build after the cutover head 05d618e2 lands. Send the class table to the planner before building. One head. Gate once before review.","target_head":"64112e4576b4c3c8fb668389786deb6b703da417","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}